eeds with 0 errors. I haven't loaded it into Grasshopper, so the async behaviour is untested. The only warnings are NU1603 package-version warnings about the Grasshopper reference.\n\n- **Pattern:** the project had only one component (`AddComponent`) and nothing async, so I took its structure: same `GH_Component` base, same category \"Bench\" with subcategory \"Data\", a fixed GUID and the same parameter registration style.\n- **Inputs and outputs:** the `Values` input is a list of numbers. The outputs are `Mean` and `StdDev`. The standard deviation is the population one (divides by N); say if you'd rather have the sample version.\n- **Async behaviour:** each solve cancels the previous run and starts the calculation on a background task, so the UI isn't blocked. When it finishes, it schedules a re-solve that publishes the result. A run that was cancelled by newer inputs never publishes.\n- **Cleanup:** removing the component from the document also cancels any run still in progress.\n- **Empty input:** an empty or missing list produces no output.","ttft_ms":3820,"type":"result","duration_ms":28811,"uuid":"6824dae3-5d49-43ea-9500-9b9e413d5854","ttft_stream_ms":3624,"time_to_request_ms":1683,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":164,"system_prompt":906,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":15,"input_attachments":136,"input_hooks":7,"tool_pool_refresh":7,"init_message":296,"engine_pickup":5,"message_prep":4,"model_config_wait":13,"autocompact":6,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":31,"message_normalization":8,"client_creation":6,"request_build":78},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":810,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":532,"time_to_request_major_faults":4834,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"queued_commands","slowest_producer_ms":113,"cpu_ms":0,"major_faults":294},"first_content_frame_ms":3624,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
